The dish looks like a square side plate, about 22 cm across. It holds roughly 14-16 roasted Brussels sprouts, mostly small, clustered on one side.

Each sprout is about 3 cm across and weighs roughly 8-10 g after roasting, so 15 sprouts come to about 130 g. They look glossy with oil, which would put them at around 70-90 kcal per 100 g. That gives about 110-120 kcal.

